## 13. Testing and Acceptance Criteria

Implement an appropriately sized automated test suite.

Consider Vitest, React Testing Library, and Playwright where compatible and useful. Choose tools based on the actual environment rather than installing all of them indiscriminately.

Prioritize tests by risk.

### Minimum Behavioral Regression Matrix

| Scenario | Expected result |
|---|---|
| User enters a prompt | Input is preserved and processed appropriately |
| User requests analysis | Structured graph and clarification results are validated |
| User answers a clarification | Answer is correctly incorporated |
| User edits a graph attribute | Intended change is reflected in the refined prompt |
| User edits a relationship | Updated relationship is preserved |
| User switches modes during a request | Stale results do not corrupt the active mode |
| User starts a second request | Earlier responses cannot overwrite the newer request |
| Image generation partially fails | Valid results remain usable and failure is reported |
| Video generation remains pending | Progress remains understandable and operation is controlled |
| Story generation completes | Output can be displayed, copied, and downloaded |
| Gemini returns malformed JSON | Failure is handled without corrupting application state |
| Gemini returns a rate-limit error | Retry handling is bounded and appropriate |
| API credentials are absent | Application displays a safe, actionable configuration error |
| User opens the app on mobile | Core controls remain accessible |
| User switches themes | Content and controls remain legible |
| User downloads generated media | Correct file content and format are delivered |

Include additional tests for important edge cases discovered during the audit.

### Verification Commands

Where the environment supports them, run:

- Dependency installation.
- Type checking.
- Linting.
- Unit tests.
- Integration tests.
- Production build.
- Browser-based smoke tests.
- Relevant accessibility checks.
